<div class="dhui-guide">

  <section class="dhui-guide-section dhui-guide-section--warning">
    <h2 class="dhui-guide-section__title">
      <i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
      Requirement: Linked Actor
    </h2>
    <p class="dhui-guide-section__body">
      To request an identify roll, <strong>the player must have a character assigned to their user
      account</strong>. The Request Identify Roll dialog only lists users who are connected, are not
      GMs, and have such a character — without one there is no inventory to read.
    </p>
    <div class="dhui-guide-steps">
      <p class="dhui-guide-steps__label">How to assign a character to a user:</p>
      <ol class="dhui-guide-steps__list">
        <li>Right-click the user name in the Players list and open <strong>User Configuration</strong>.</li>
        <li>Pick the actor for that user. The user must have ownership of that actor.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Save Changes</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dhui-guide-section">
    <h2 class="dhui-guide-section__title">
      <i class="fas fa-eye-slash"></i>
      Hiding an Item (Mystify)
    </h2>
    <p class="dhui-guide-section__body">
      Works on <strong>weapons, armor, loot and consumables</strong>. Right-click the item in an
      actor's inventory and choose <strong>Mystify Item</strong>, or open the item sheet and use the
      <strong>&#8942;</strong> header menu. A dialog lets you set the masked name, description and
      icon that players will see.
    </p>
    <p class="dhui-guide-steps__note">
      Nothing is written over the item itself. The real name, image and description stay in the
      document at all times — the mask is presentation only, applied when the sheet renders. Disable
      the module and every item is immediately back to normal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="dhui-guide-section">
    <h2 class="dhui-guide-section__title">
      <i class="fas fa-eye"></i>
      Revealing an Item (Identify)
    </h2>
    <p class="dhui-guide-section__body">
      To reveal an item straight away, right-click it and choose <strong>Identify Item</strong>, or
      use the <strong>&#8942;</strong> menu on its sheet and confirm with <strong>Identify</strong>.
      To make the players earn it, send them a roll instead — see below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="dhui-guide-section">
    <h2 class="dhui-guide-section__title">
      <i class="fas fa-dice-d20"></i>
      Requesting an Identify Roll
    </h2>
    <p class="dhui-guide-section__body">
      Open <strong>Identify Items</strong> from the Daggerheart Menu, or run
      <strong>Identify.Open()</strong> in a macro.
    </p>
    <div class="dhui-guide-steps">
      <ol class="dhui-guide-steps__list">
        <li>Pick the player on the left. Their unidentified items are listed below.</li>
        <li>Click an item to select it. The magnifier opens its real sheet if you need a look.</li>
        <li>Pick a trait and a difficulty, and toggle <strong>Advantage</strong> or
            <strong>Disadvantage</strong> if the situation calls for it.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Send to Player</strong>. A prompt appears on their screen.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="dhui-guide-steps__note">
        The player only ever sees the masked name and icon in that prompt. On a success the item
        reveals itself; on a failure it stays hidden and you can try again later.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dhui-guide-section">
    <h2 class="dhui-guide-section__title">
      <i class="fas fa-users"></i>
      Party Sheet Items
    </h2>
    <p class="dhui-guide-section__body">
      Unidentified items sitting on a <strong>party actor</strong> are offered too, marked with a
      purple edge and a group icon. Any player can be asked to identify one — the item never has to
      be on their own character. The party actor qualifies when
      <strong>every player owns it</strong>, either through default ownership set to Owner or an
      explicit Owner grant for each player.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="dhui-guide-section">
    <h2 class="dhui-guide-section__title">
      <i class="fas fa-user-secret"></i>
      Result Privacy
    </h2>
    <p class="dhui-guide-section__body">
      In module settings, <strong>Identify Result Privacy</strong> controls who learns the outcome.
      <strong>Public</strong> (the default) shows the result to the whole table.
      <strong>Private</strong> keeps the roll, the result message and the sound between the player
      who rolled and the GM. This setting is GM-only and applies to every request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="dhui-guide-section">
    <h2 class="dhui-guide-section__title">
      <i class="fas fa-sliders-h"></i>
      Defaults and Sounds
    </h2>
    <p class="dhui-guide-section__body">
      <strong>Configure Default Masks</strong> in module settings sets the masked name, description
      and icon suggested for each item type, so mystifying is usually one click and done. The same
      dialog sets the success and failure sounds played when a roll resolves.
    </p>
  </section>

</div>
